WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.320
A spinning wheel needs no
twist to keep it turning,

2
00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.450
only to change its spin.

3
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.590
Now picture an old well.

4
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:11.750
A rope is wound around a heavy
drum, with a bucket on the end.

5
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:12.820
Let go.

6
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.960
As the bucket falls,
the drum begins to spin,

7
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:17.830
faster and faster.

8
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.210
Even with a frictionless axle, the bucket
speeds up more gently than a dropped

9
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.250
stone.

10
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.790
Why does it fall with less
than free-fall acceleration?

11
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.980
In this mission, you'll meet the
turning version of Newton's second law.

12
00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:34.010
Then you'll link a falling
mass to a turning drum,

13
00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.100
and solve for both together.

14
00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:40.960
Your mission: explain why the bucket
speeds up more gently than a freely falling

15
00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:41.400
one.
